  "dom_id": "step-q3889",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/406bfedb1113d8e953fcac9739a144027a592ac5d7e2409604147a1b7f258a02.png)\n\nThe graph above is a translation of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$ Identify the equation that generated the graph.",
  "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $4$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+1}-4.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/df21cfbd88c5090a58fc45bf36eaf6b83a51fcf8476e0fa492290b48882ede7d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\sqrt{x+1}-4.$",
